   "source": [
    "# 06 — Social Media Integration & Text Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "## What to do\n",
    "Analyze diabetes-related social media text and integrate insights with health data findings.\n",
    "\n",
    "## What you'll learn\n",
    "- Text preprocessing and cleaning\n",
    "- Sentiment analysis\n",
    "- Topic modeling\n",
    "- Word frequency analysis\n",
    "- Compare social discussion themes with health risk factors\n",
    "- Bridge structured health data with unstructured text"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1: Setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "from collections import Counter\n",
    "import re\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "\n",
    "# NLP libraries\n",
    "import nltk\n",
    "from nltk.corpus import stopwords\n",
    "from nltk.tokenize import word_tokenize\n",
    "from nltk.sentiment import SentimentIntensityAnalyzer\n",
    "\n",
    "# Download required NLTK data\n",
    "nltk.download('punkt', quiet=True)\n",
    "nltk.download('stopwords', quiet=True)\n",
    "nltk.download('vader_lexicon', quiet=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style='whitegrid')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('NLP libraries loaded!')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2: Sample social media data\n",
    "\n",
    "**Action:** Create sample diabetes-related social media posts.\n",
    "**Insight:** In production, you would scrape real social media with proper permissions. This demonstrates the workflow."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sample social media posts about diabetes (for demonstration)\n",
    "sample_posts = [\n",
    "    'Just got diagnosed with type 2 diabetes. Going to start exercising more and eat healthier.',\n",
    "    'My blood sugar levels are finally under control! Diet and exercise really work!',\n",
    "    'Struggling with diabetes management. It\\'s so hard to give up sugary foods.',\n",
    "    'Great news! My HbA1c dropped from 8.5 to 7.2. Medication and lifestyle changes paying off!',\n",
    "    'Feeling frustrated with diabetes. Insulin injections are painful and expensive.',\n",
    "    'Starting a new exercise routine to improve my health and manage diabetes better.',\n",
    "    'Love my diabetes support group! So helpful to connect with others going through this.',\n",
    "    'BMI is down 5 pounds this month. One step closer to better health.',\n",
    "    'The diabetes diagnosis was shocking but I\\'m committed to making changes.',\n",
    "    'Exercise and healthy eating have been transforming my energy levels!',\n",
    "    'Doctor says my cardiovascular health is improving. Less risk for heart disease now.',\n",
    "    'Meal planning is exhausting but necessary for managing my condition.',\n",
    "    'Celebrating small wins! Another week of good blood glucose readings.',\n",
    "    'The stress and anxiety about diabetes complications keeps me up at night.',\n",
    "    'Grateful for modern medicine. My insulin pump makes life so much easier.',\n",
    "    'Weight loss journey: 20 pounds down and feeling so much better!',\n",
    "    'Hypertension and diabetes together is tough. Managing multiple conditions.',\n",
    "    'My family\\'s support has been incredible throughout this journey.',\n",
    "    'New fitness challenge: trying to walk 10,000 steps every day!',\n",
    "    'Depression and diabetes go hand in hand. Mental health matters too.'\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "posts_df = pd.DataFrame({'text': sample_posts})\n",
    "posts_df['post_id'] = range(len(posts_df))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Sample social media data: {len(posts_df)} posts')\n",
    "print('\\nFirst 3 posts:')\n",
    "for i in range(3):\n",
    "    print(f'{i+1}. {posts_df.iloc[i][\\'text\']}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3: Text preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "**Action:** Clean text by removing punctuation, lowercasing, and stopwords.\n",
    "**Insight:** Clean text improves quality of analysis and reduces noise."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def preprocess_text(text):\n",
    "    # Lowercase\n",
    "    text = text.lower()\n",
    "    # Remove special characters\n",
    "    text = re.sub(r'[^a-zA-Z0-9\\s]', '', text)\n",
    "    # Tokenize\n",
    "    tokens = word_tokenize(text)\n",
    "    # Remove stopwords\n",
    "    stop_words = set(stopwords.words('english'))\n",
    "    tokens = [w for w in tokens if w not in stop_words and len(w) > 2]\n",
    "    return ' '.join(tokens)\n",
    "\n",
    "posts_df['cleaned_text'] = posts_df['text'].apply(preprocess_text)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Text preprocessing complete!')\n",
    "print('\\nExample:')\n",
    "print(f'Original: {posts_df.iloc[0][\\'text\'][:60]}...')\n",
    "print(f'Cleaned: {posts_df.iloc[0][\\'cleaned_text\'][:60]}...')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4: Sentiment analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Action:** Analyze sentiment (positive, negative, neutral) for each post.\n",
    "**Insight:** Sentiment shows emotional tone. High negativity may indicate patient concerns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sia = SentimentIntensityAnalyzer()\n",
    "\n",
    "sentiments = []\n",
    "for text in posts_df['text']:\n",
    "    scores = sia.polarity_scores(text)\n",
    "    sentiments.append(scores)\n",
    "\n",
    "sentiment_df = pd.DataFrame(sentiments)\n",
    "posts_df = pd.concat([posts_df, sentiment_df], axis=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Classify sentiment\n",
    "def classify_sentiment(compound):\n",
    "    if compound >= 0.05:\n",
    "        return 'positive'\n",
    "    elif compound <= -0.05:\n",
    "        return 'negative'\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        return 'neutral'\n",
    "\n",
    "posts_df['sentiment_class'] = posts_df['compound'].apply(classify_sentiment)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Sentiment Analysis Results:')\n",
    "print(posts_df[['text', 'sentiment_class', 'compound']].head(10))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5: Sentiment distribution\n",
    "\n",
    "**Action:** Visualize sentiment distribution across posts.\n",
    "**Insight:** Reveals overall emotional tone of diabetes discussion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 5))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sentiment counts\n",
    "sentiment_counts = posts_df['sentiment_class'].value_counts()\n",
    "sentiment_counts.plot(kind='bar', ax=axes[0], color=['green', 'red', 'gray'])\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Sentiment Distribution')\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('Sentiment')\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Count')\n",
    "axes[0].tick_params(axis='x', rotation=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compound scores histogram\n",
    "axes[1].hist(posts_df['compound'], bins=15, edgecolor='black', color='steelblue')\n",
    "axes[1].axvline(0, color='red', linestyle='--', label='Neutral')\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Distribution of Sentiment Scores')\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('Compound Score (-1 to 1)')\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('Frequency')\n",
    "axes[1].legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Average sentiment: {posts_df[\"compound\"].mean():.3f}')\n",
    "print(f'Positive posts: {(posts_df[\"sentiment_class\"] == \"positive\").sum()}')\n",
    "print(f'Negative posts: {(posts_df[\"sentiment_class\"] == \"negative\").sum()}')\n",
    "print(f'Neutral posts: {(posts_df[\"sentiment_class\"] == \"neutral\").sum()}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6: Word frequency analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**Action:** Count most common words in all posts.\n",
    "**Insight:** Shows which topics/words dominate diabetes discussion."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Extract all words from cleaned text\n",
    "all_words = []\n",
    "for text in posts_df['cleaned_text']:\n",
    "    words = text.split()\n",
    "    all_words.extend(words)\n",
    "\n",
    "word_freq = Counter(all_words)\n",
    "top_words = dict(word_freq.most_common(15))\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Top 15 Most Frequent Words:')\n",
    "for word, count in top_words.items():\n",
    "    print(f'  {word}: {count}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualize\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
    "plt.barh(list(top_words.keys())[::-1], list(top_words.values())[::-1], color='teal')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Frequency')\n",
    "plt.title('Top 15 Most Frequent Words in Diabetes Posts')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7: Identify key health-related themes\n",
    "\n",
    "**Action:** Search for mentions of specific health factors.\n",
    "**Insight:** Maps social media discussion to clinical risk factors."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "health_themes = {\n",
    "    'Exercise': ['exercise', 'walk', 'activity', 'fitness', 'training'],\n",
    "    'Diet': ['diet', 'eating', 'food', 'sugar', 'meal'],\n",
    "    'Weight': ['weight', 'bmi', 'pounds', 'losing', 'slim'],\n",
    "    'Blood Sugar': ['blood', 'glucose', 'sugar', 'hba1c'],\n",
    "    'Medication': ['insulin', 'medication', 'medicine', 'pill', 'drug'],\n",
    "    'Mental Health': ['depression', 'anxiety', 'stress', 'mood'],\n",
    "    'Complications': ['hypertension', 'heart', 'cardiovascular', 'complications'],\n",
    "    'Support': ['support', 'family', 'doctor', 'help', 'group']\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "theme_mentions = {}\n",
    "for theme, keywords in health_themes.items():\n",
    "    mentions = 0\n",
    "    for text in posts_df['cleaned_text']:\n",
    "        for keyword in keywords:\n",
    "            if keyword in text:\n",
    "                mentions += 1\n",
    "                break\n",
    "    theme_mentions[theme] = mentions\n",
    "\n",
    "theme_df = pd.DataFrame(list(theme_mentions.items()), columns=['Theme', 'Mentions']).sort_values('Mentions', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Health-Related Themes in Social Media:')\n",
    "display(theme_df)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "plt.barh(theme_df['Theme'], theme_df['Mentions'], color='steelblue')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Number of Posts Mentioning Theme')\n",
    "plt.title('Health-Related Themes in Diabetes Discussion')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 8: Sentiment by theme\n",
    "\n",
    "**Action:** Analyze sentiment for each health theme.\n",
    "**Insight:** Shows which topics generate positive vs negative emotions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sentiment_by_theme = {}\n",
    "\n",
    "for theme, keywords in health_themes.items():\n",
    "    theme_posts = posts_df.copy()\n",
    "    # Filter posts mentioning this theme\n",
    "    theme_mask = theme_posts['cleaned_text'].str.contains('|'.join(keywords), regex=True)\n",
    "    theme_sentiment = theme_posts[theme_mask]['compound'].mean()\n",
    "    sentiment_by_theme[theme] = theme_sentiment\n",
    "\n",
    "sentiment_theme_df = pd.DataFrame(list(sentiment_by_theme.items()), columns=['Theme', 'Avg_Sentiment']).sort_values('Avg_Sentiment', ascending=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Average Sentiment by Health Theme:')\n",
    "display(sentiment_theme_df.round(4))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "colors = ['green' if x > 0 else 'red' for x in sentiment_theme_df['Avg_Sentiment']]\n",
    "plt.barh(sentiment_theme_df['Theme'], sentiment_theme_df['Avg_Sentiment'], color=colors)\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Average Sentiment Score')\n",
    "plt.axvline(0, color='black', linestyle='-', linewidth=0.8)\n",
    "plt.title('Sentiment by Health Theme')\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 9: Integration insights\n",
    "\n",
    "**Action:** Summarize key findings from social media analysis.\n",
    "**Insight:** Connects social discussion patterns with clinical risk factors from our modeling."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print('='*70)\n",
    "print('SOCIAL MEDIA ANALYSIS SUMMARY')\n",
    "print('='*70)\n",
    "print(f'\\nTotal posts analyzed: {len(posts_df)}')\n",
    "print(f'Average sentiment: {posts_df[\"compound\"].mean():.3f} ({\"Positive\" if posts_df[\"compound\"].mean() > 0 else \"Negative\"})\n')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Key Themes Discussed:')\n",
    "for i, row in theme_df.head(5).iterrows():\n",
    "    print(f'  - {row[\"Theme\"]} ({row[\"Mentions\"]} mentions)')\n",
    "\n",
